0,Agusan language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agusan_language,"Language family. Austronesian. Malayo-Polynesian. Philippine.Variously: msm – Agusan, Omayamnon mbd – Dibabawon mqk – Rajah Kabunsuwan. Glottolog. east2478. Agusan is a Manobo language of northeastern Mindanao in the Philippines. Distribution and dialects.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
1,"Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan Language... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mqk/,"Rajah Kabunsuwan Manobo is a stable indigenous language of the Philippines. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
2,Rajah Kabunsuwan Manobo - mqk (Austronesian) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/mqk/,"Rajah Kabunsuwan Manobo (mqk) is part of the Austronesian family and Austronesian, Malayo-Polynesian, Greater Central Philippine, Manobo, Central, East class.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
3,"Manobo, Rajah Kabungsuan in Philippines people... | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/14512/RP,"Learn about the Manobo, Rajah Kabungsuan in Philippines people group. Profiles include statistics, text, photo, map, progress indicator and language resources.Rajah Kabungsuan Manobo; Rajah Kabunsuan. Population this Country. 12,000.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
4,"Rajah Kabunsuwan Manobo language. Evangelism tools, church...",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/mqk,"Rajah Kabunsuwan Manobo language and dialect information. Audio Bible stories and lessons. Download free evangelism resources, MP3s, audio bible study tools, language/dialect information.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
5,manobo primer.indd,http://s3images.coroflot.com/user_files/individual_files/349768_CkzAWXSE2FuPGWR6bYRxepec1.pdf,"Manobo, dibabawon (mandaya, dibabaon, debabaon) manobo, rajah kabunsuwan.Manobo vocal music consists of ritual songs that are narrative songs, lullabies, and songs of nature. An important song type is the epic song Owaging/Uwahingen.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
6,"Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan | Articles - PuertoParrot.com",https://www.puertoparrot.com/articles/manobo-rajah-kabunsuwan?lang=en,"Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan. Manobo simply means “people” or “person”; alternate names include Manuvu and Minuvu.The Rajah Kabunsuwan Manobo are found in Surigao del Sur, mostly in the south. Their language is 80% mutually intelligible with Dibabawon.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
7,(PDF) An Archival Study on the Linguistic State of Obo Manobo and...,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/396030352_An_Archival_Study_on_the_Linguistic_State_of_Obo_Manobo_and_Kinamiging_Manobo,"Manobo Dibabawon, and Manobo Rajah Kabunsuwan, while the southcentral speakers consist of Ata.At the same. time, Manobo Rajah Kabunsuwan is considered vigorous, and Obo Manobo and Manobo Kinamiging. are considered threatened.","Manobo, Rajah Kabunsuwan",Austronesian
